        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "7b64b7dc1ca5a3258e34fb2f8001a39d11131a1b",
            "parents": [
                "75a27e2616caac2f4f0910762498abe7e0af2972"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/89/77289/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                "username": "jagpalgill"
            },
            "createdOn": 1737590086,
            "author": {
                "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                "username": "jagpalgill"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 105,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "ModbusDevice, SubType, and ConnectionType all need to be combined into a single type field.\n\nModbusi2cFlowmeter\n\nfor example.  Creating these subtypes removes our ability in the future to branch off.  Maybe flow meters need to be handled by a different service than general modbus devices?  Keeping them all in the top level type lets us do that.\n\n(added later) see note below.  We might need to be even more device specific in the type if modbus doesn't define standard register definitions"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 105,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "nit, take out the word \"rack\" nothing about the modbus device itself makes it a \"rack\" pump.  That's a location identifier."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 136,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I see a lot of stuff here that's related to the modbus serial link itself that I would've expected to go into the modbusdetect (which should be called modbuslink) type."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 136,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "ModbusRTUDetect and ModbusRTUDevice are 2 different schemas, are you suggesting to create a common schema def for common properties and reuse it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 136,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I have created a new schema SerialPort and moved link related properties into that configuration object.\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/80242"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 150,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Are these registers standard things defined by the modbus specification?  If so, can we give them names?\n\nIf these are per-device register settings, they belong in c++ code and we need a \"type\" that matches the specific device.  WE shouldn't be encoding long lists of registers in json config."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 150,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> Are these registers standard things defined by the modbus specification?  If so, can we give them names?\n\nRegister as a concept is standard. Refer to Section 4.3 Data Model\n> \n> If these are per-device register settings, they belong in c++ code and we need a \"type\" that matches the specific device.  WE shouldn't be encoding long lists of registers in json config.\n\nSpecific sensors can vary between different devices, thats the reason i have just added the general register properties here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 164,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "These need to be an array of structs, like the other sensors are."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 164,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 190,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Same with all these.  These are trying to encode device-specific registers into an EM json config.  These need to just be mapped in the modbus daemon.  You can have a trivial lookup table of device/register map that's very similar."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/modbus_device.json",
                    "line": 190,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Are you referring to the firmware register? If yes, then that needs to be explicitly called out as i am trying to keep the property name common across all modbus rtu devices."
                }
            ],
